WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.717
Tessera turns cheap

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:03.321
ESP32 touchscreens

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.217
into drag-and-drop

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:05.609
Home Assistant dashboards

00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:07.765
Tessera is open-source

00:00:07.576 --> 00:00:08.720
firmware layered on

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.017
ESPHome plus a

00:00:09.829 --> 00:00:11.019
Home Assistant screen

00:00:10.831 --> 00:00:12.045
manager that builds

00:00:11.857 --> 00:00:13.331
multi-page dashboards

00:00:13.143 --> 00:00:14.769
for 2.8-inch to

00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:17.187
10.1-inch ESP32 touch

00:00:16.999 --> 00:00:18.484
panels from CYD

00:00:18.706 --> 00:00:20.238
Guition and Waveshare

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.347
without YAML or

00:00:21.194 --> 00:00:22.196
MQTT

00:00:22.726 --> 00:00:24.082
Dashboards are edited

00:00:23.893 --> 00:00:24.919
with drag and

00:00:24.731 --> 00:00:25.862
drop inside Home

00:00:25.674 --> 00:00:26.417
Assistant

00:00:26.488 --> 00:00:27.183
and pushed to

00:00:26.995 --> 00:00:28.351
screens over Wi-Fi

00:00:28.162 --> 00:00:29.412
without reflashing

00:00:29.942 --> 00:00:31.215
The Tessera firmware

00:00:31.027 --> 00:00:31.781
adds a layer

00:00:31.593 --> 00:00:33.149
to ESPHome firmware

00:00:32.961 --> 00:00:34.222
for display management

00:00:34.352 --> 00:00:35.519
touchscreen handling

00:00:35.614 --> 00:00:36.887
dashboard rendering

00:00:36.947 --> 00:00:37.701
tiles

00:00:37.725 --> 00:00:39.222
plugins and more

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.764
Full story on

00:00:40.575 --> 00:00:41.471
the dashboard
